Kifaru-X

TARGET:
ExampleBank

MALWARE:
PhantomLoader
The example is synthetic.

10. Topic Detection
Instead of reading thousands of messages manually, NLP can identify emerging topics.

Example:
Topic A → ransomware
Topic B → stolen credentials
Topic C → phishing
Topic D → vulnerability exploitation
Topic E → malware development
A topic can be monitored over time.

If a topic suddenly increases:
Week 1: 12 mentions
Week 2: 17 mentions
Week 3: 31 mentions
Week 4: 96 mentions
the system can generate an emerging-threat signal.

A signal is not automatically proof of a campaign.

11. Sentiment vs Threat Intent
Traditional sentiment analysis asks:
Is the text positive, neutral, or negative?

Threat intelligence requires different questions:
Is the text operational?

Is it discussing a vulnerability?

Is it claiming a breach?

Is it advertising malware?

Is it discussing infrastructure?

Threat-intelligence NLP therefore needs intent classification, not merely sentiment classification.

12. African Multilingual Threat Intelligence
